content:
Aisha: FYI onboarding for Hastro is hitting a preflight fanout issue during warmup — lots of 429s and they say the SDK fires preflight for every page load. @Devon can you eyeball?
Devon: saw the trace, thanks. Likely a stampede from parallel init + short-lived ephemeral tokens. Quick wins: memoize token client-side, add jittered backoff for preflight, and reduce concurrent preflight on SPA cold-starts.
Aisha: here is what their frontend does (simplified):
```js
async function init() {
  await Promise.all([preflight(), preflight(), preflight(), preloadModels()]);
}
function preflight(){
  return fetch('/api/preflight', { headers: { Authorization: `Bearer ${token}` } });
}
```
They also refresh token on every route change which is... verbose.
Marco: yep that pattern will thrash our preflight quota. Two routes: 1) infra side — temp quota bump + warmup window, 2) client side — reduce calls. We usually recommend single preflight with LRU for session.
Aisha: tried changing client to single-call but they still do background refreshs via service-worker. Any advice to recommend?
Devon: ask them to switch to memoized token + conditional refresh: only refresh if token age > 70% TTL. Add splay on refresh across clients. Example:
```js
let tokenPromise = null;
function getToken(){
  if (!tokenPromise) tokenPromise = fetchToken().finally(()=> setTimeout(()=> tokenPromise=null, 60_000));
  return tokenPromise;
}
// preflight calls use getToken() so only 1 inflight refresh per tab/session
```
Aisha: applied similar change and added exponential backoff to preflight calls. Logs show 429s dropped from ~180/min to ~12/min in the next 30s. Pasting snippet:
```
[2025-11-03T14:02:23Z] preflight 200 init-first
[2025-11-03T14:02:27Z] preflight 429 warmup-2
[2025-11-03T14:02:45Z] preflight 200 retry-backoff
```
Marco: nice improvement. We should still offer them a short warmup quota bump for first 48h while they roll out changes. I can open a support action with ops. @OnboardBot can you create a temp-capacity request tag HASTRO-ONB-52?
OnboardBot: Created ticket #HASTRO-ONB-52 for temporary capacity bump (48h), owner: Marco, ETA: 2h.
Devon: also verify they send x-client-id header on preflight so we can attribute requests to a single client for better caching on our edge. If missing we'll treat them as anonymous and apply stricter per-IP shaping.
Aisha: they were missing x-client-id, sending sample: `curl -H "x-client-id: hastro-web-1" /api/preflight`. After adding it, our tracing shows grouped warmup requests under one client.
Marco: final checklist for CS handoff: 1) client token memoization + splay/backoff, 2) service-worker refresh debounce, 3) x-client-id present, 4) ops temp bump (ticket HASTRO-ONB-52), 5) monitor dashboard for 2h, rollback plan if errors spike.
Aisha: thanks — I'll message the customer with the checklist and confirm once they deploy.
Devon: LMK if they need a small SDK patch we can ship to make token memoization opt-in.
Aisha: will do, closing this thread once they confirm deployment. :thumbsup:
